":"Neither the server nor the clients are responding.","option_b":"Neither the server nor the clients is responding.","option_c":"Despite of the delay, neither the server nor the clients are responding.","option_d":"The team discussed about why neither the server nor the clients are responding."},{"id":"ev-grammar-23","category":"english_verbal","subcategory":"Grammar","question_text":"ev-grammar-23: Choose the grammatically correct sentence.","options":["The quality of the samples was satisfactory.","The quality of the samples were satisfactory.","Despite of the delay, the quality of the samples was satisfactory.","The team discussed about why the quality of the samples was satisfactory."],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"The first sentence follows standard agreement, tense and usage rules.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"The quality of the samples was satisfactory.","option_b":"The quality of the samples were satisfactory.","option_c":"Despite of the delay, the quality of the samples was satisfactory.","option_d":"The team discussed about why the quality of the samples was satisfactory."},{"id":"ev-grammar-24","category":"english_verbal","subcategory":"Grammar","question_text":"ev-grammar-24: Choose the grammatically correct sentence.","options":["She explained the procedure clearly and concisely.","The sentence contain error ev-grammar-24-1.","Despite of the delay, she explained the procedure clearly and concisely.","The team discussed about why she explained the procedure clearly and concisely."],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"The first sentence follows standard agreement, tense and usage rules.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.2,"option_a":"She explained the procedure clearly and concisely.","option_b":"The sentence contain error ev-grammar-24-1.","option_c":"Despite of the delay, she explained the procedure clearly and concisely.","option_d":"The team discussed about why she explained the procedure clearly and concisely."},{"id":"ev-grammar-25","category":"english_verbal","subcategory":"Grammar","question_text":"ev-grammar-25: Choose the grammatically correct sentence.","options":["By next June, they will have completed the project.","By next June, they will has completed the project.","Despite of the delay, by next june, they will have completed the project.","The team discussed about why by next june, they will have completed the project."],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"The first sentence follows standard agreement, tense and usage rules.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.3,"option_a":"By next June, they will have completed the project.","option_b":"By next June, they will has completed the project.","option_c":"Despite of the delay, by next june, they will have completed the project.","option_d":"The team discussed about why by next june, they will have completed the project."},{"id":"db-1-1","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"SQL Filtering","question_text":"Which clause filters rows before grouping?","options":["WHERE","HAVING","ORDER BY","DISTINCT"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"WHERE filters input rows; HAVING filters groups.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.4,"option_a":"WHERE","option_b":"HAVING","option_c":"ORDER BY","option_d":"DISTINCT"},{"id":"db-1-2","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Aggregation","question_text":"Which clause filters aggregate groups?","options":["HAVING","WHERE","SELECT DISTINCT","LIMIT"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"HAVING is evaluated on groups after GROUP BY.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.5,"option_a":"HAVING","option_b":"WHERE","option_c":"SELECT DISTINCT","option_d":"LIMIT"},{"id":"db-1-3","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Keys","question_text":"What property must every primary-key value have?","options":["It is unique and non-null","It may repeat","It must be text","It must reference another table"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"A primary key uniquely identifies a row and cannot be null.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"It is unique and non-null","option_b":"It may repeat","option_c":"It must be text","option_d":"It must reference another table"},{"id":"db-1-4","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Foreign Keys","question_text":"What does a foreign key primarily enforce?","options":["Referential integrity","Sort order","Column encryption","Query caching"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"It constrains values to referenced candidate-key values.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"Referential integrity","option_b":"Sort order","option_c":"Column encryption","option_d":"Query caching"},{"id":"db-1-5","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Normalization","question_text":"Which normal form removes partial dependency on a composite key?","options":["Second normal form","First normal form","Third normal form","BCNF only"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"2NF removes partial dependencies on a candidate key.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.2,"option_a":"Second normal form","option_b":"First normal form","option_c":"Third normal form","option_d":"BCNF only"},{"id":"db-1-6","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Transactions","question_text":"Which ACID property ensures committed data survives failure?","options":["Durability","Atomicity","Isolation","Consistency"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Durability preserves committed changes.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.3,"option_a":"Durability","option_b":"Atomicity","option_c":"Isolation","option_d":"Consistency"},{"id":"db-1-7","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Transactions","question_text":"Which ACID property makes a transaction all-or-nothing?","options":["Atomicity","Isolation","Durability","Availability"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Atomicity prevents partial transactions.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.4,"option_a":"Atomicity","option_b":"Isolation","option_c":"Durability","option_d":"Availability"},{"id":"db-1-8","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Indexes","question_text":"What is the usual trade-off of adding an index?","options":["Faster reads but extra storage and write cost","Faster writes with no cost","Automatic normalization","Guaranteed uniqueness for every index"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Indexes accelerate matching reads but must be maintained on writes.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.5,"option_a":"Faster reads but extra storage and write cost","option_b":"Faster writes with no cost","option_c":"Automatic normalization","option_d":"Guaranteed uniqueness for every index"},{"id":"db-1-9","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"JOIN","question_text":"Which join retains every row from the left table?","options":["LEFT JOIN","INNER JOIN","CROSS JOIN","SELF JOIN"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"LEFT JOIN preserves all left rows.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"LEFT JOIN","option_b":"INNER JOIN","option_c":"CROSS JOIN","option_d":"SELF JOIN"},{"id":"db-1-10","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"NULL","question_text":"Which predicate correctly tests missing SQL values?","options":["IS NULL","= NULL","== NULL","NULL()"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"NULL uses IS NULL because equality with NULL is unknown.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.1,"option_a":"IS NULL","option_b":"= NULL","option_c":"== NULL","option_d":"NULL()"},{"id":"db-1-11","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Grouping","question_text":"A query selects department and COUNT(*). What else is normally required?","options":["GROUP BY department","ORDER BY department","HAVING department","DISTINCT COUNT"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Non-aggregated selected columns normally belong in GROUP BY.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.2,"option_a":"GROUP BY department","option_b":"ORDER BY department","option_c":"HAVING department","option_d":"DISTINCT COUNT"},{"id":"db-1-12","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Isolation","question_text":"What anomaly is prevented when a transaction cannot read uncommitted changes?","options":["Dirty read","Lost index","Dead column","Schema drift"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"Dirty reads observe another transaction's uncommitted work.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.3,"option_a":"Dirty read","option_b":"Lost index","option_c":"Dead column","option_d":"Schema drift"},{"id":"db-1-13","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Query Logic","question_text":"COUNT(column_name) differs from COUNT(*) because it does what?","options":["Ignores NULL values in that column","Counts distinct values only","Counts tables","Returns text"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"COUNT(column) ignores NULL; COUNT(*) counts rows.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.4,"option_a":"Ignores NULL values in that column","option_b":"Counts distinct values only","option_c":"Counts tables","option_d":"Returns text"},{"id":"db-1-14","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Set Operations","question_text":"What does UNION do by default?","options":["Removes duplicate rows","Keeps all duplicates","Joins columns by keys","Updates both queries"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"UNION applies duplicate elimination; UNION ALL does not.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9.5,"option_a":"Removes duplicate rows","option_b":"Keeps all duplicates","option_c":"Joins columns by keys","option_d":"Updates both queries"},{"id":"db-1-15","category":"database_technical","subcategory":"Subqueries","question_text":"A correlated subquery is evaluated with reference to what?","options":["A row from the outer query","Only system tables","A stored procedure","An index page"],"correct_answer":"A","explanation":"It references values supplied by the outer query.","estimated_time_seconds":60,"difficulty":9,"option_a":"A row from the outer query","option_b":"Only system tables","option_c":"A stored procedure","option_d":"An index page"}]$diagnostic$::jsonb) as x(id text,question_text text,category text,subcategory text,difficulty numeric,option_a text,option_b text,option_c text,option_d text,correct_answer char(1),explanation text,estimated_time_seconds integer) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,category=excluded.category,subcategory=excluded.subcategory,difficulty=excluded.difficulty,option_a=excluded.option_a,option_b=excluded.option_b,option_c=excluded.option_c,option_d=excluded.option_d,correct_answer=excluded.correct_answer,explanation=excluded.explanation,estimated_time_seconds=excluded.estimated_time_seconds,active=true;
